# FOG Agent release signing roots.
#
# Every certificate in this file is trusted by THIS BUILD to have signed a
# release manifest (design 0015 section 3). Nothing else is.
#
# It is deliberately empty in the repository. A build made from a plain
# checkout therefore trusts no signing root and refuses every self-update,
# reporting "no signing root" rather than a signature failure -- which is
# the right behavior for a binary nobody signed for.
#
# A release build, or a lab build, replaces this file before compiling:
#
#     build/mint-signing-ca.sh --install    # lab CA, writes here
#
# Two roots are better than one. Losing the only root that a deployed
# fleet trusts means those agents can never be updated again by any
# mechanism they carry; a second root, generated at the same time and
# stored somewhere else entirely, costs one more block in this file.
